Z||000002||JoBy||12-14-2001||10:50 AM||||I live in Sweden, so you can probalby find someone closer to help you.<P>It is a very simple interface. Only one transistor and two resistors.<P> <IMG SRC="http://w1.601.telia.com/~u60113744/software/winaldl/interface.gif"> <P>This is the cable I use:<P> <IMG SRC="http://w1.601.telia.com/~u60113744/software/winaldl/mycable.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://w1.601.telia.com/~u60113744/software/winaldl/myaldl.jpg"> <P>You can read a lot more about the software on the thirdgen message board.<P>160 baud ALDL Scanner.. A Reality!  <A HREF="http://www.thirdgen.org/messgboard/Forum10/HTML/002113.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thirdgen.org/messgboard/Forum10/HTML/002113.html</A> <P>160 buad ALDL Scanner... A Reality! Part ll <A HREF="http://www.thirdgen.org/messgboard/Forum10/HTML/002368.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thirdgen.org/messgboard/Forum10/HTML/002368.html</A> <P>Winaldl Cable <A HREF="http://www.thirdgen.org/messgboard/Forum10/HTML/002444.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thirdgen.org/messgboard/Forum10/HTML/002444.html</A> <P>FREE scan software for TBI !!!  <A HREF="http://www.thirdgen.org/messgboard/Forum11/HTML/002597.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thirdgen.org/messgboard/Forum11/HTML/002597.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>Jonas Bylund<BR><A HREF="http://w1.605.telia.com/~u60505093/index.htm" TARGET=_blank>     <IMG SRC="http://w1.601.telia.com/~u60113742/forum/sig.JPG">     </A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||12-14-2001||11:52 AM||||Cool! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Your program has some fantastic tuning power, well done!<P>------------------<BR>Bryce<BR> <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/jbnash/nashcosig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||12-15-2001||11:19 PM||||I got it working!!! This is a very cool program that seems to do everything a scanner will do, only in a <B>nice</B> windows interface, PLUS it will log everything to a file. There are also some tables for the O2, BLM and Int that I haven't gotten into yet. They look like they would be useful with tuning for modifications. Anyone with access to a laptop (or a computer in the garage) can have a scanner for a fraction of the cost of a traditional one. Great job, Jonas!!! Thanks!!!<P>A couple of notes that might save others some time and money I wasted. I made the connecting cable the first time in less than an hour with less than $5 worth of Radio Shack parts (listed below) and some speaker wire I already had. It worked, but I didn't realize it because...<P><B>Note 1:</B> You need a 10k resistor between terminals A and B on the ALDL connector to get meaningful data. This puts the ECM in ALDL mode, in normal mode you will get 5 bytes of data that probably mean something but the program doesn't understand it. <P>I didn't know this so I was fiddling with it and broke one of the transistor leads off. Back to Radio Shack... There was some discussion on using a 15 pack of NPN transistors (276-1617) that Radio Shack sells for $2.49. That sounded like a good idea since I'd already broke the single one I got for .69 (MPS2222A), so I got them.<P><B>Note 2:</B> I could not get it to work with the 276-1617 transistors. I don't know if it was my laptop or the Fiero ECM, but it wouldn't work. Someone on the other board even said the package marking was wrong for the terminals so I even hooked it up that way, still no-go.<P>One more trip back to Radio Shack (good thing I like driving the Fiero   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) to get another MPS2222A. I put it all together, including a jumper with a 10k resistor between the A and B terminals that I had added in the last attempts, and it worked.<P><BR>Part - Radio Shack # - Price:<BR>MPS2222A transistor - 276-2009 - .69<BR>10k resistors (5 pack) - 271-1335 - .69<BR>D-sub 9 pin <B>female</B> connector - 276-1538C - 1.49<BR>D-sub Housing - 276-1539D - 1.49<P>Edit: I forgot to mention, I tinned the ends of the wires with solder to plug into the ALDL connector. <p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 12-15-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000005||JoBy||12-17-2001||07:09 AM||||I just wanted to add that this is the info I used to add support for the 1227170 ECM:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ecmguy.geo/diagnostics/7170aldl.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/ecmguy.geo/diagnostics/7170aldl.html</A> <P>If you look at flag-data ( bytes 1, 15,16 and 17 ) you see that some are active 0 and some active 1. Some of the flags in the program might have a misleading description. A checked ckeckbox indicates a 1 in that position. I don't have access to a 7170 ECM so if you find some texts that should be changed you can e-mail me joby.teknik@telia.com<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonas Bylund<BR><A HREF="http://w1.605.telia.com/~u60505093/index.htm" TARGET=_blank>       <IMG SRC="http://w1.601.telia.com/~u60113742/forum/sig.JPG">       </A>||||reg||7
